WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:03.503
- Hey.

00:00:04.657 --> 00:00:06.893
- [Kelly] Thank you for being here.

00:00:06.893 --> 00:00:07.726
- Thank you for having me back,

00:00:07.726 --> 00:00:09.545
I had such a great time last time.

00:00:09.545 --> 00:00:10.378
- I was excited to have you back,

00:00:10.378 --> 00:00:11.670
but then I was more excited

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:12.720
because I know you're friends with Jessie,

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.197
so we were like "Wait, we know you sing,

00:00:14.197 --> 00:00:15.450
"do you wanna sing on the show?"

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.778
And then you said, "Yes."

00:00:16.778 --> 00:00:17.611
- Of course I wanted to sing.

00:00:17.611 --> 00:00:18.930
- I know, I was very excited.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.010
Have you ever sang that song?

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:20.843
I hadn't.

00:00:20.843 --> 00:00:21.676
- I've never sang that song.

00:00:21.676 --> 00:00:23.100
No, I think I'd heard it before.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.420
I mean, I'm sure I've heard it in a movie

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:25.440
or something like that.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.790
- But I wasn't familiar with it.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:27.720
And I love Sinatra,

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.973
I'm familiar with a lot of his stuff.

00:00:28.973 --> 00:00:30.450
- Yeah, we were talking about
how you love his catalog.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.283
- Yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:32.116
- It's great.

00:00:32.116 --> 00:00:32.949
- Me too, me too.

00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:34.950
It is a weird song that a father
and daughter sing together.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.261
- It's super creepy.
- Yeah.

00:00:36.261 --> 00:00:37.399
- Yeah.

00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:38.232
It's very creepy that a father

00:00:38.232 --> 00:00:39.345
and daughter are singing like,

00:00:39.345 --> 00:00:40.387
"Yeah, I just wanna hang
out with you and I love you.

00:00:40.387 --> 00:00:42.253
"We're gonna have drinks together."

00:00:42.253 --> 00:00:43.653
- [Kelly] (laughs) Yeah.
- It's like, "Okay, bro."

00:00:43.653 --> 00:00:44.486
- [Kelly] It's a little inappropriate.

00:00:44.486 --> 00:00:45.319
- Calm down.

00:00:45.319 --> 00:00:46.152
- But I love the song,

00:00:46.152 --> 00:00:47.040
and I just let it go.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.020
So, have you ever thought
of doing an album?

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:49.947
- I have, yeah.

00:00:49.947 --> 00:00:50.947
I-

00:00:50.947 --> 00:00:51.780
- 'Cause I want you to do,

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.120
I told him my goal for him, for me,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.280
is to be in some kind of Rat Pack movie,

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.320
or if they redo "White Christmas."

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.760
We were talking about
that with Jessie earlier.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.720
- Yeah, yeah, I would love to do that.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.006
Listen, I-

00:01:02.006 --> 00:01:02.839
- You have the perfect voice for that.

00:01:02.839 --> 00:01:03.672
- Thank you, I really appreciate that.

00:01:03.672 --> 00:01:04.950
- Yeah.
- I love singing so much.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.210
I've gotten to do Broadway a couple times,

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.526
like I've told you,

00:01:07.526 --> 00:01:08.910
but that's a very
Broadway type of singing,

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.610
and I would love to do
stuff that's more mainstream

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.443
or whatever it is.
- Yeah.

00:01:12.443 --> 00:01:13.680
- Even if it's like Rat Packy,

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.752
that kind of an era,

00:01:14.752 --> 00:01:16.500
all that stuff is golden to me,

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.640
just a bunch of bangers.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.839
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:18.839 --> 00:01:19.971
(audience applauding)

00:01:19.971 --> 00:01:20.804
I'm just saying,

00:01:20.804 --> 00:01:21.637
you and Michael Bublé,

00:01:21.637 --> 00:01:23.010
and me and Jessie,

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:23.960
getting to do, "White
Christmas," all over again.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:24.793
- Oh my God, me and Bublé,

00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:26.266
- [Kelly] What?
What?

00:01:26.266 --> 00:01:27.099
- and you and Jessie?

00:01:27.099 --> 00:01:27.932
- What?
- Come on.

00:01:27.932 --> 00:01:28.765
- I think this is a great idea.

00:01:28.765 --> 00:01:29.910
- Let's call up Bublé immediately.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.385
- I was just like

00:01:31.385 --> 00:01:32.218
"Wait, this would be
a really great movie."

00:01:32.218 --> 00:01:34.044
Anyway, throwing it out there.
(Zachary laughing)

00:01:34.044 --> 00:01:35.550
So St. Patrick's Day is tomorrow,

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:36.383
do you celebrate?

00:01:36.383 --> 00:01:37.216
Do you get into that?

00:01:37.216 --> 00:01:40.557
- I do, I have a lot of Irish blood in me.

00:01:40.557 --> 00:01:41.390
- I do too.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.223
- Any the Irish people in the audience?

00:01:42.223 --> 00:01:43.056
(audience cheering)
- Me.

00:01:43.056 --> 00:01:44.038
- All right, good.

00:01:44.038 --> 00:01:44.871
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:45.704
- Get that Irish blood, yeah.

00:01:45.704 --> 00:01:47.784
- I found out, 27%, 23andMe, thank you.

00:01:47.784 --> 00:01:50.203
- Did you know you were
Irish at all before that?

00:01:50.203 --> 00:01:51.465
- I did, I did, yes, yes.

00:01:51.465 --> 00:01:52.298
- [Zachary] Okay, okay, yeah.

00:01:52.298 --> 00:01:53.131
- But I didn't know the percentage.

00:01:53.131 --> 00:01:54.065
- [Zachary] Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:54.065 --> 00:01:56.070
- So we have a good bit of
Irish in my family blood,

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.440
and my grandma was super
into St. Patrick's Day.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.210
We grew up in Ventura, California,

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:02.220
and every St. Patrick's Day

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.020
there's a St. Patrick's Day parade.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:04.853
- Yeah.

00:02:04.853 --> 00:02:07.080
- And my grandmother was a part
of the Irish-American club,

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.510
and I don't know why or how

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:10.560
they got their hands on this,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:11.640
but they had a float,

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.730
and that float was like
a big truck flatbed,

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.730
and they had this massive
inflatable green pig.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.865
And I don't know why. (laughs)

00:02:19.865 --> 00:02:22.470
I don't know if there's a pig

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.933
that's associated with St.
Patrick or Ireland at all.

00:02:25.933 --> 00:02:27.300
- I feel it's the little
Lucky Charm kinda guy,

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.431
not a pig.

00:02:28.431 --> 00:02:29.264
Wait-

00:02:29.264 --> 00:02:30.097
- Well, yeah, that could be a leprechaun.

00:02:30.097 --> 00:02:30.930
- Yeah, leprechaun, leprechaun.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.623
- An inflatable leprechaun
would've made a lot more sense.

00:02:32.623 --> 00:02:34.230
But they have a giant inflatable pig,

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:35.063
and it's green.
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:35.063 --> 00:02:37.050
So they got it and they
put it on a flatbed,

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.430
and then we would just ride it down-

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:39.263
- They were like "This is free."

00:02:39.263 --> 00:02:40.230
- Totally, exactly.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.640
Hey, you guys want a green pig?

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.440
Yeah, anything green, it's fine.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.820
And so, yeah, we would ride along

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:45.780
with that float every year.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.540
When I was really cool I
roller bladed next to it.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:49.440
- Oh my God, you were one of those guys.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.273
- I was one of those kids.

00:02:50.273 --> 00:02:52.020
- Don't worry about it.
- Totally, yeah, yeah.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:52.853
All the way down the parade route too.

00:02:52.853 --> 00:02:53.905
- I was too.

00:02:53.905 --> 00:02:54.738
(both laughing)

00:02:54.738 --> 00:02:55.571
Total nerd.

00:02:55.571 --> 00:02:56.404
- Yeah, yeah, totally.

00:02:56.404 --> 00:02:57.540
Yeah, so that was,

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.040
a lot of fun memories
with the family that way.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.240
- That's so cool.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.073
All right.

00:03:01.073 --> 00:03:01.906
Well last time we were here

00:03:01.906 --> 00:03:03.330
we talked about your move to Texas,

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.230
how's that going?

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.063
- It's good.

00:03:05.063 --> 00:03:06.300
- 'Cause you're doing a whole
musical thing there, right?

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.590
- I'm trying to build a campus, yeah.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.690
I'm trying to build
multiple campuses really

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:10.950
kind of around the country where

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.470
basically places where artists,

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:14.970
arts and the people who work in the arts

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.560
and sciences of entertainment

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.200
have a place to work and
live and play together,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.120
and kind of create together,

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.920
and build a better life for
as many of us as possible.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:23.753
- Networking.

00:03:23.753 --> 00:03:24.769
- Yeah.

00:03:24.769 --> 00:03:25.650
And in Austin, it's such a groovy town,

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:26.483
I mean I'm sure you spent
plenty of time there.

00:03:26.483 --> 00:03:27.316
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:27.316 --> 00:03:28.350
- Very music centric,

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.760
and so I think a music campus there

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:30.780
would be really awesome.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.613
- Yeah.

00:03:31.613 --> 00:03:33.705
- Amphitheaters to play music in,

00:03:33.705 --> 00:03:35.700
and also recording
facilities to make music in,

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.990
and then a bunch of places for all of us

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.460
to live while you're doing it.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.380
'Cause often times, don't you guys go,

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.134
you got to a specific place,

00:03:42.134 --> 00:03:45.090
I know various artists will go

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.410
down to a Caribbean Island,

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.240
and go record an entire album

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.260
in that mindset.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.603
You go to some retreat
or something like that.

00:03:50.603 --> 00:03:51.610
- I think No Doubt did that.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:52.443
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:52.443 --> 00:03:53.460
- They did a Caribbean Island-

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.540
- The Joe Bros did too I'm pretty sure.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.915
- [Kelly] Rocky steady or something.

00:03:55.915 --> 00:03:56.814
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:56.814 --> 00:03:57.647
Ryan Tedder, he does
that stuff all the time.

00:03:57.647 --> 00:03:59.001
- Yeah.

00:03:59.001 --> 00:04:00.774
I just go to my closet in my house.

00:04:00.774 --> 00:04:02.070
(both laughing)

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.000
- You're like I don't need it, I'm fine.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.267
I'm fine.

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:05.130
- I'll take this staycation.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.020
I can be inspired anywhere.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.250
- Yeah, yeah, totally.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.690
- It is nice though to have,

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.000
whenever I do go to a studio I like,

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.830
I like for the place to feel vibey.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:16.547
And so what you're
creating does inspire you.

00:04:16.547 --> 00:04:17.380
- Yeha, yeah.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:18.870
- And it's also really cool

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.040
because a lot of people that are creative

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.000
don't know how to get started,

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.054
or don't know, they don't
know people to meet up,

00:04:24.054 --> 00:04:24.887
the guitarist or the vocalists,

00:04:24.887 --> 00:04:25.720
or whatever, writers.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:26.553
And that's a really cool place.

00:04:26.553 --> 00:04:27.827
You can do it in Atlanta, Texas.

00:04:27.827 --> 00:04:28.660
- That's the thing.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:29.493
And if you can bring people together,

00:04:29.493 --> 00:04:31.200
I mean it's almost like,

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.033
not that I lived then,

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:34.560
but the village in New York in the 60's,

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.880
it was just nothing but artists,

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.100
and everybody was kind of
living next to each other

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.270
or on top of each other,

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.860
and poets would bump into other writers

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.330
or directors or actors,

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:43.350
and musicians.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:44.264
- How many great things came from that.

00:04:44.264 --> 00:04:45.097
- There was synergy, exactly.

00:04:45.097 --> 00:04:46.080
And it just happened naturally,

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.150
and that's the kind of enviornment
I wanna create for sure.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.050
- I love that.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.670
So will you be using your new studio

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:51.870
to work on the "Chuck" reboot?

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.651
Because we heard the reboot
might happen, like a movie?

00:04:54.651 --> 00:04:56.756
- Listen, did you guys want more "Chuck?"

00:04:56.756 --> 00:04:57.589
(audience cheering)

00:04:57.589 --> 00:04:58.422
- What?

00:04:58.422 --> 00:04:59.940
What?

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.140
- I know, right?

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:01.973
Look at that baby.

00:05:01.973 --> 00:05:03.157
Just a baby.

00:05:03.157 --> 00:05:04.800
- I know, but it's so cool.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.870
I mean it's such a cult following.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:07.703
- Yeah.

00:05:07.703 --> 00:05:08.536
- Chuck, I mean,

00:05:08.536 --> 00:05:09.611
I'm telling you-

00:05:09.611 --> 00:05:10.444
- I know.

00:05:10.444 --> 00:05:11.550
- People in masses would
come to see this movie.

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:12.930
- Listen, I've been trying for years.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:14.340
I was trying to make a "Chuck" movie

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.080
even before we finished
making the TV show.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.940
It's getting closer-

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:18.773
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:05:18.773 --> 00:05:19.606
- I'm getting closer.

00:05:19.606 --> 00:05:20.439
- Don't let us down.

00:05:20.439 --> 00:05:21.570
(both laughing)

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.403
- The pressure.

00:05:23.251 --> 00:05:25.260
Look, Josh Schwartz and Chris Fedak,

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:26.880
who are the writer and
creator of the show,

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.760
they're on board, I just
gotta get the powers that be,

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.190
meaning the folks at Warner Brothers

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:33.863
television and film to kind of help

00:05:33.863 --> 00:05:35.340
let's put this thing together,

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:36.720
but all the cast is all ready to go.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.830
Everybody's ready to go,

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:38.820
we just need a script,

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.290
and we need the money,

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.502
and the green light.

00:05:41.502 --> 00:05:43.290
- Yeah, you need backing for it.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:44.123
- Yeah, exactly.

00:05:44.123 --> 00:05:44.956
- Here's the thing though,

00:05:44.956 --> 00:05:46.740
you have leverage 'cause we all want it.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.030
So do it.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:48.863
- So do it.

00:05:48.863 --> 00:05:49.696
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:49.696 --> 00:05:50.630
You heard it.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:51.463
Kelly said do it, so we'll do it.

00:05:51.463 --> 00:05:52.296
(audience applauding)

00:05:52.296 --> 00:05:54.180
- Everyone is excited
that "Shazam" is back,

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.550
so was it fun to kind of
get in superhero mode again?

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:57.383
- Oh, absolutely.

00:05:57.383 --> 00:05:58.436
- [Kelly] Yeah?

00:05:58.436 --> 00:06:01.200
- I mean it's such an
incredible gift of a job.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.033
- [Kelly] Yeah,

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:02.866
- Ever since I was a little kid

00:06:02.866 --> 00:06:03.870
I dreamt about being an actor,

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:04.890
and I get to do that,

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.330
and that just blows my mind still.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.760
And I also always dreamt
about being a superhero,

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.703
I think we all do-

00:06:09.703 --> 00:06:10.536
- Yeah.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:11.369
- When we're kids,

00:06:11.369 --> 00:06:12.202
and I never really let go of that.

00:06:12.202 --> 00:06:13.110
(Kelly laughing)

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:15.570
But the cool thing is I
love Tom Hanks in "Big,"

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.070
and I loved Christopher
Reeves in "Superman,"

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:19.440
and I get to play the lovechild of both.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.700
- What a great, yeah.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:21.866
- It really is.

00:06:21.866 --> 00:06:22.699
It's "Big" meets "Superman,"

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:23.532
and it's so fun,

00:06:23.532 --> 00:06:25.770
and I just get to tap into my inner child

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:27.810
that I never really grew out of

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:28.950
on a daily basis,

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:30.240
and just bring that to life.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.680
And the fact that I got to do that once

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:32.640
was already incredible,

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:33.690
now I get to do it again,

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:35.340
and we get to bring the whole family,

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:37.380
the whole Shazamily back together.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:38.760
All the rest of the cast.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.200
- I love that, sharing of the,

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.287
I'm not ruining it, watch
the first one, spoiler alert,

00:06:42.287 --> 00:06:44.160
but you share the powers.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.810
I think that that's such a great lesson.

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:46.643
- [Zachary] Yeah.

00:06:46.643 --> 00:06:48.390
- It's such a great message overall.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:51.470
And also in this new one you
get to body slam Helen Miren.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:52.303
- Oh yeah.

00:06:52.303 --> 00:06:53.190
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:54.023
- Yeah.

00:06:54.023 --> 00:06:55.395
Let me tell you guys-

00:06:55.395 --> 00:06:56.228
- [Kelly] A dame.

00:06:56.228 --> 00:06:57.061
You got to body slam a dame.

00:06:57.061 --> 00:06:59.280
- Yeah, I get to suplex
a dame into concrete.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:00.477
- It's a big fight.

00:07:00.477 --> 00:07:01.989
- Oh, it's so dope.

00:07:01.989 --> 00:07:03.006
(audience laughing)

00:07:03.006 --> 00:07:04.260
This scene, that scene
right there is so fun,

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.820
that was the first scene
we got to work together on.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.980
It was like three pages of
us just having dialogue,

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:09.727
and I was so like "What am I doing?

00:07:09.727 --> 00:07:11.460
"This is Dame Helen Miren right now."

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.293
And she's-

00:07:12.293 --> 00:07:13.380
- Right after that
everything goes to hell.

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:14.490
- And then everything goes super south,

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:15.323
yeah, goes super south.

00:07:15.323 --> 00:07:16.603
But she's the coolest.

00:07:16.603 --> 00:07:21.150
I think she, yeah, she's
the undamiest dame,

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.260
she doesn't throw it around.

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:25.921
She's just like a really chill human

00:07:25.921 --> 00:07:27.810
who wants to roll up her sleeves,

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:29.190
and jump in the sandbox and have fun,

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:30.796
and that's the kind of actor
you wanna work with always.

00:07:30.796 --> 00:07:31.629
- Yeah.

00:07:31.629 --> 00:07:32.462
- Yeah, yeah.

00:07:32.462 --> 00:07:33.295
And she's an icon on top of that.

00:07:33.295 --> 00:07:34.128
- I already loved her,

00:07:34.128 --> 00:07:35.326
but now I love her more
from that knowledge.

00:07:35.326 --> 00:07:36.159
- [Zach] Yeah.

00:07:36.159 --> 00:07:38.040
- And she, this fight is incredible.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.150
- Yeah.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:41.310
- So you also, amongst all your jobs,

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:43.166
had time to publish a book last year.

00:07:43.166 --> 00:07:43.999
- I did, yeah.

00:07:43.999 --> 00:07:45.420
- So it's called "Radical Love

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.340
Learning to Accept Yourself and Others."

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:49.350
This is so important, can I tell you why?

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:50.183
- Yeah.

00:07:50.183 --> 00:07:51.180
- Because I read a bit,

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.810
and I think it's, for me to have a six

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:55.800
and eight year old kid, right,

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.030
and they go through things

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.620
like bullying at school, whatever,

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.112
things that happen,

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:02.880
learning disability, things like that,

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.130
and they can struggle, right?

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:08.020
When they see someone
that's a superhero to them

00:08:08.942 --> 00:08:11.250
owning that life can be hard

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.470
and a struggle for even Shazam-

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.303
- Yeah.

00:08:14.303 --> 00:08:16.620
- You don't know how cool that is for...

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.540
And I'm trying not to cry,

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:19.800
but you don't know how cool that is.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.632
I was talking to Anthony Macky
about this the other day.

00:08:21.632 --> 00:08:24.330
It's so cool that you all
are superheros to these kids,

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:25.890
but then you own things publicly

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:28.950
that are vulnerable things
that you don't have to,

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:29.790
you don't have to share,

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.166
but it's so cool that you do

00:08:31.166 --> 00:08:33.750
'cause it makes them feel normal,

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:37.006
and it makes them feel
like they have a voice.

00:08:37.006 --> 00:08:38.683
You know what I'm saying?

00:08:38.683 --> 00:08:39.516
- I do.

00:08:39.516 --> 00:08:40.440
- I don't know if you're
doing it for that reason,

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:42.129
and I'm not crying.

00:08:42.129 --> 00:08:43.620
- We're not crying, we're not crying.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:44.700
- Ignore this.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:45.930
Allergies.

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:47.520
Anyway, it's just really important

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:48.780
to sit there with your kids,

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:50.137
and be like just so you know,

00:08:50.137 --> 00:08:51.750
this guy struggles too.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:53.550
You said you had such a
hard say the other day.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:54.450
He struggles too,

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:55.440
and he's got a whole book about it.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.040
And it really does make
a difference to kids

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.990
that you're their hero,
looking up to them,

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:01.823
that you're honest about that.

00:09:01.823 --> 00:09:02.700
- I receive that.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:03.600
I really receive that.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:04.874
- [Kelly] Yeah, it's so cool.

00:09:04.874 --> 00:09:05.707
(audience applauding)

00:09:05.707 --> 00:09:06.540
- But-

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:07.950
- 'Cause it's very vulnerable
like what you talk about.

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:10.740
- Yeah, but I think, I really do believe,

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:12.120
and I've said this many times before,

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:13.710
vulnerability is a superpower.

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:16.350
The more we can all allow
ourselves to be seen,

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:18.870
the more you are cuing other people

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.310
it's okay to be seen.

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:21.143
- Yeah.

00:09:21.143 --> 00:09:22.020
- And then it's a ripple effect.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.310
And opening and being honest,

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:26.280
and being transparent, it's
a really beautiful thing

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:27.908
because we're all wearing

00:09:27.908 --> 00:09:28.741
so many masks we don't even realize

00:09:28.741 --> 00:09:32.100
how often we're not being our
truest most authentic self

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:33.750
because we're trying to survive.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.500
And society has all these conditions.

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:39.240
In middle school this horribleness
starts with being cool,

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.910
finding a click, being
accepted by the cool kids,

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:43.260
or whatever the heck that means.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:44.130
I wish I could go back,

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:45.453
and shake my young self,

00:09:46.415 --> 00:09:47.248
and say don't think about that,

00:09:47.248 --> 00:09:48.081
don't worry about that,

00:09:48.081 --> 00:09:48.914
go do your studies-

00:09:48.914 --> 00:09:50.580
- You're gonna peak in high school.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:52.440
- Yes, exactly, don't peek in high school,

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:53.288
bad place to be.

00:09:53.288 --> 00:09:56.070
(Kelly laughing)

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:57.720
listen, I mean I basically,

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:58.800
the book gets into it,

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.000
but about six years ago,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.620
when I made my move out to Austin,

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.000
I had this complete mental breakdown,

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.200
I didn't wanna live anymore,

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.255
and I didn't know why.

00:10:05.255 --> 00:10:06.900
And thank God I had family

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:08.460
and friends around me
that were supporting me,

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:11.250
I got myself into this
life-saving therapy.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.560
And after, I was still doing this therapy,

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.030
I was finishing it up

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:17.640
when I got the audition for
another role in "Shazam."

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:20.370
I sent my tape in, they liked it so much

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.117
they said "Hey, actually
he could be Shazam,

00:10:22.117 --> 00:10:23.460
"we haven't casted that yet."

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:24.960
Then they auditioned me for Shazam,

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:25.830
and then I got the part.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.240
All that happened in like one week

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:28.680
after having this breakthrough,

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:31.068
finally recognizing that I
never loved myself before.

00:10:31.068 --> 00:10:31.901
- Yeah.

00:10:31.901 --> 00:10:32.734
- And I had this breakthrough,

00:10:32.734 --> 00:10:33.570
I was like "Oh my God,
I need to love myself."

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:34.500
Oh, now I'm gonna cry.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.090
And so all of a sudden-

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:37.975
- 'Cause you're not
really able to love others

00:10:37.975 --> 00:10:38.905
until you can love yourself.

00:10:38.905 --> 00:10:40.200
- You can't, you can't, you can't.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.255
Not fully.

00:10:41.255 --> 00:10:42.588
We can do bits of that-

00:10:42.588 --> 00:10:43.922
- [Kelly] Play the role.

00:10:43.922 --> 00:10:46.080
- But if you wanna fully
completely love people,

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.490
the more kind you are with yourself

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:48.540
the kinder you can be with others.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.710
The more patient you are with yourself

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.000
the more patient you can be with others.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.260
And so I learned these things.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:54.150
And then on the heels of
that I booked this job,

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:56.850
and because of that I felt,

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:58.148
I know I don't have to do this,

00:10:58.148 --> 00:10:59.640
but I actually do.

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:00.930
I need to tell people

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.780
the only reason I got
to wear this super suit,

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:05.820
I literally went from
suicide to superhero,

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:07.230
and it was all because I learned

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:09.090
that I'm allowed to love myself,

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:10.440
and I'm worthy of that love,

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.215
and we are all worthy of that love.

00:11:12.215 --> 00:11:13.048
(audience applauding)

00:11:13.048 --> 00:11:15.660
- Worth is such a hard thing for so many.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:16.493
- Yeah, yeah.

00:11:16.493 --> 00:11:17.850
- Especially if you didn't
learn that at a younger age

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:18.810
and it carries over.

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:21.360
- And if I could have
gotten out of my own way,

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.870
and been practicing a
lot more true gratitude

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:27.150
for what I had and where I had been,

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:29.100
and by the way that
all, again, starts with

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:31.200
you have to love the life that you have.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.260
You have to know that
you are worth loving,

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:35.970
even if you haven't accomplished

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:37.800
all the things you think
you're supposed to accomplish

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:38.633
in this world.

00:11:38.633 --> 00:11:40.710
That will never get you there.

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:43.200
External validation does not provide that,

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.760
that has to come from within.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.920
And so all of that external validation

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:49.015
that I had counted on, like this job,

00:11:49.015 --> 00:11:50.910
being an actor and getting hired,

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:52.350
and being able to play that role

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:53.700
or this role or whatever,

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:56.670
no matter, it would bougie
me for a little while,

00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:58.410
but then it eventually tapers off.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:11:59.970
So you can't depend on that.

00:11:59.970 --> 00:12:01.170
You've got to recognize

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:03.930
that it's spending time with yourself,

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:06.390
loving yourself, all these
things that I didn't understand

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.470
when I was in Austin,

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:08.880
and so it just spiraled.

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.200
I just went all the way down,

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.615
I felt like a complete failure,

00:12:11.615 --> 00:12:15.120
and I needed people around me
to remind me that I wasn't,

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:18.300
but that I do think that the irony is that

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:21.810
when you do the work the
success actually comes

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:24.841
even more easily because
now you're prepared.

00:12:24.841 --> 00:12:25.920
- You're almost open and inviting it in.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:26.753
- Yes.

00:12:26.753 --> 00:12:27.586
- Yeah.

00:12:27.586 --> 00:12:28.440
- And I really do believe in that adage

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:29.880
God doesn't give you
more than you can handle,

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:31.590
the universe doesn't give
you more than you can handle.

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:33.668
- Sometimes I have arguments
with God about that.

00:12:33.668 --> 00:12:34.501
(Zachary laughing)

00:12:34.501 --> 00:12:35.415
- Sure, but you're still here.

00:12:35.415 --> 00:12:36.360
- I'm like are you sure?

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.193
- You're still here,

00:12:37.193 --> 00:12:38.026
and you're still alive.

00:12:38.026 --> 00:12:38.859
- Yeah, yeah.

00:12:38.859 --> 00:12:39.692
- You're bringing joy to so many people.

00:12:39.692 --> 00:12:40.525
- Yeah.

00:12:40.525 --> 00:12:41.358
- I think that, yes, I'm with you,

00:12:41.358 --> 00:12:42.191
sometimes you're like

00:12:42.191 --> 00:12:43.140
I don't think I can handle this right now.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:44.581
- Yeah.

00:12:44.581 --> 00:12:46.710
- But what seemed like a
mountain turns into a mole hill

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:47.550
in the distance-

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:48.383
- [Kelly] Hindsight.

00:12:48.383 --> 00:12:49.511
- You're like I did handle
it, I did handle it.

00:12:49.511 --> 00:12:51.414
- I love you and I love you-

00:12:51.414 --> 00:12:52.247
- I love you.

00:12:52.247 --> 00:12:53.080
- for doing this book.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:53.913
(Zachary laughing)

00:12:53.913 --> 00:12:54.870
And helping people with
what you've learned,

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:56.850
and sharing that knowledge
'cause not everybody

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:58.830
is capable of going where you went,

00:12:58.830 --> 00:12:59.940
and having those therapies.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:01.198
Not everybody can afford
all that kind of stuff.

00:13:01.198 --> 00:13:02.031
- Exactly.

00:13:02.031 --> 00:13:03.420
- It's awesome to have
all that for people.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:04.530
Let's do another break.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:06.270
Zachary's book is called "Radical Love

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:07.800
Learning to Accept Yourself and Others,"

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:08.640
it's out now.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.490
And "Shazam Fury of the Gods"
is in theaters tomorrow,

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:13.290
you have to go see it, it's so good.

